			"Message": "refactor(Air): Standardize TODO comments to FUTURE naming convention\n\nThis commit renames remaining TODO comments to FUTURE throughout the Air daemon codebase to align with the project's naming conventions for planned future enhancements.\n\nChanges made:\n- WaitForShutdownSignal.rs: Updated 4 TODO references to FUTURE (signal source verification, configurable shutdown timeout, SIGHUP handling, graceful timeout)\n- Downloader/mod.rs: Updated 5 TODO references to FUTURE (per-host concurrent limits, adaptive concurrency, chunk size optimization, priority queue, chunk verification)\n- Library.rs: Updated 1 TODO reference to FUTURE (IPv4/IPv6 binding support)\n\nThis follows the cleanup work in the previous commit which removed placeholder TODOs and adds lint attributes, ensuring consistent terminology for features planned for future implementation.",
