			],
			"Message": "refactor(Air): Standardize field naming to singular form in ApplicationState\n\nThis commit refactors the naming convention in the Air daemon's ApplicationState module, changing plural field names to singular form for improved consistency and clarity.\n\n**Field Renames in ApplicationState:**\n- `ActiveRequests` → `ActiveRequest`\n- `Connections` → `Connection`\n- `BackgroundTasks` → `BackgroundTask`\n\n**Field Renames in PerformanceMetrics:**\n- `TotalRequests` → `TotalRequest`\n- `SuccessfulRequests` → `SuccessfulRequest`\n- `FailedRequests` → `FailedRequest`\n\n**Field Renames in ConnectionHealthReport:**\n- `TotalConnections` → `TotalConnection`\n- `HealthyConnections` → `HealthyConnection`\n- `StaleConnections` → `StaleConnection`\n- `ConnectionsByType` → `ConnectionByType`\n\n**Code Updates:**\n- Updated all variable usages throughout ApplicationState to match new singular naming (e.g., `Connections` → `Connection`, `Requests` → `Request`)\n- Updated Binary.rs shutdown statistics logging to use new field names\n- Updated AirVinegRPCService.rs gRPC response and metrics mapping to use singular field names\n\n**Impact**: This naming standardization follows the singular form convention used elsewhere in the Air codebase and improves code readability by using singular field names to represent single collection containers.",
			"SHA": "221fc793414206124fbf7171a3441a20facb7989"
		},
